### Email Verification API Tests
### For use with VS Code REST Client extension or similar tools

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@email = test@example.com
@userName = testuser
@password = TestPass123!

### 1. Register a new user (will send verification email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{userName}}",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Expected Response:
### {
###   "message": "Registration successful! Please check your email to verify your account.",
###   "email": "test@example.com",
###   "requiresEmailVerification": true
### }

###

### 2. Try to login before email verification (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "rememberMe": false
}

### Expected Response (401 Unauthorized):
### {
###   "message": "Please verify your email address before logging in. Check your inbox for the verification link."
### }

###

### 3. Resend verification email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/resend-verification-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### Expected Response:
### {
###   "message": "If the email exists in our system and is not yet verified, a verification link has been sent."
### }

###

### 4. Verify email (replace TOKEN_FROM_EMAIL with actual token from email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "token": "TOKEN_FROM_EMAIL"
}

### Expected Response:
### {
###   "message": "Email verified successfully! You can now log in."
### }

###

### 5. Login after email verification (should succeed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "rememberMe": false
}

### Expected Response (200 OK):
### {
###   "accessToken": "jwt_token...",
###   "refreshToken": "refresh_token...",
###   "tokenType": "Bearer",
###   "expiresIn": 3600,
###   "userId": "...",
###   "userName": "testuser",
###   "email": "test@example.com",
###   "role": "User"
### }

###

### 6. Try to verify already verified email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "token": "ANY_TOKEN"
}

### Expected Response:
### {
###   "message": "Email is already verified. You can now log in."
### }

###

### 7. Test forgot password (sends reset email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### Expected Response:
### {
###   "message": "If the email exists in our system, a password reset link has been sent."
### }

###

### 8. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###
